<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pura Meru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1720</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pura Meru is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple in Cakranegara on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, built in 1720 under the Balinese rulers of the island. It is the largest temple on Lombok, with courtyards holding tiered meru shrines of eleven, nine and seven roofs dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahma">Brahma</a>. It served the Hindu Balinese community that ruled western Lombok.</p></div>
